      "name": "Resonant Wildlife",
      "type": "feature",
      "_id": "eClfhi4sfUs7rjk5",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>Once per scene, mark 1 Stress to call nearby wildlife around a target within Far range. They make an Instinct Reaction Roll (14). On a failure, they mark 1 Stress and have disadvantage on their next attack against the hunter before the end of the hunter’s next spotlight. On a success, the animals scatter without mechanical effect. If that attack does not occur by the deadline, the disadvantage ends. This uses wildlife already present; it does not summon an Actor.</p>",
